  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 3002.28 \"Reasonably available control technology\" or \"RACT\" for the purposes of Env-A 3000 through Env-A 3200 means \"RACT\" as defined in RSA 125-J:1,XXV, namely \"the lowest emission limitation that a stationary source is capable of meeting by the application of control technology that is reasonably available considering technological and economic feasibility.\"\n\nSource. #6441, EXEMPT, eff 1-21-97",
